pst-numeric: changes

1.5    2026/11/22  first release on CTAN
                 - regress centres and scales x for polynomials and the
                   transforms, so fits far from x = 0 work with single
                   precision reals (pst-fit's precision test: degree 4 at
                   x = 293..302 failed before, degree 2 was off in the 4th
                   digit); /coef and /cov are transformed back
                 - regress options for pst-fit: /xtrans, /ytrans, /yback
                   (CustomFit), /drop (leave out invalid points, counted
                   in /dropped), /tval (tvp), /bignum, /exact, /exactt;
                   in bignum mode the t value now comes from reals unless
                   /exactt is given (seconds faster)
                 - new results /xbar /ybar /sxx /syy /sxy /xused /yused
                 - regevalt, regcit, regpit: evaluation in the space of
                   the fit (plotcoord=trans)
                 - setbnx: a real to a bignum with all its binary digits
                 - regShow words xbar ybar sxx syy sxy dropped ciw
                 - 71 new tests

1.4.1  2026/11/22  (not released on CTAN)
                 - regress: option /yoffset c fits y - c and adds c back
                   (y = c + a x^b, y = c + a e^(bx), a Gauss curve on a
                   baseline), as pst-fit's Yint does; regeval, regci,
                   regpi and \psNumericRegression take it into account
                 - the documentation no longer says that /intercept is
                   pst-fit's Yint: it fixes the constant term in the
                   space of the fit, which matches Yint only for
                   polynomials without a constant term (ReduceOrder)
                 - 12 new tests (1524 in all)

1.4  2026/11/22  (not released on CTAN)
                 - presentation: number formats (numFormat=auto, fixed,
                   sci; numDigits, numTrim, numDecimal, sciStyle) for
                   \psNumericShow; \psNumericMatrix lays out matrices,
                   vectors and tensor slices with delimiters and decimal
                   alignment; \psNumericRegression prints a fit,
                   \psNumericRegPlot plots it with its bands, data and
                   residuals; \psNumericDef computes a result once
                 - regression (the GLLSR code of pst-fit's example):
                   regress, linreg, regeval, regci, regpi with
                   polynomials, own basis functions, power, exp, log,
                   reciprocal and Gauss models, weights, a fixed
                   intercept, exact t values and studentized residuals
                 - statistics: listmin, listmax, listsum, mode, wmean,
                   skewness, kurtosis, quantile, histogram; rngseed,
                   rnguniform, rngnormal; fgauss (Gauss-Legendre)
                 - new part tensor (option tensor): tensors of any rank,
                   touter, tcontract, tdot, teinsum, tpermute, tsym,
                   tantisym, tlevi, tdelta, tcross, tlower, traise and more
                 - matrices: mchol, mqr, msvd, msingular, mpinv, mnull,
                   meigvec, meigsymv, mexp, mpow, mkron, mdiag
                 - special: digamma, betafn, lnbeta, choose, gammainc,
                   gammaincc, betainc, besseli, besselk, bessely; t,
                   chi-squared, F, exponential, binomial and Poisson
                   distributions (pdf, cdf, inv)
                 - bignums: powmodbn, isprime, factor
                 - calc now loads special; procedures that raise an
                   error close their dictionaries first
                 - 623 new tests (1512 in all)

1.3  2026/11/21  (not released on CTAN)
                 - bignums: ebn, rootbn, minbn, maxbn, idivbn, modbn; a
                   faster division by small integers makes exp, sin, atan
                   and the other series up to 8 times faster
                 - matrices: meig (every eigenvalue of any square matrix),
                   mlu, mrank, mtrace, mnorm, mnorm1, mnorminf, mcond
                 - complex numbers: csin, ccos, ctan, csinh, ccosh, ctanh
                   and their inverses casin, cacos, catan, casinh,
                   cacosh, catanh
                 - calc: polyinterp, spline, splineval, fmin, fderiv,
                   fsolve, mean, median, variance, stddev, covariance,
                   correlation, oderk4, odesolve, fft, ifft
                 - new part special (option special): gamma, lngamma,
                   erf, erfc, normpdf, normcdf, norminv, besselj
                 - 308 new tests (889 in all); new sections in the manual
                   and the showcase

1.2  2026/11/21  (not released on CTAN)
                 - the library is now the PSTricks package pst-numeric
                   (tex/pst-numeric.tex, latex/pst-numeric.sty), with
                   options to load only some parts, \pstNumeric,
                   \psNumericShow and a manual
                 - every name is defined in the dictionary tx@NumericDict
                   instead of userdict; Load.ps opens it, so code that
                   starts with (Load.ps) run works unchanged
                 - each part is a dvips header in dvips/, generated by
                   source/make_headers.py
                 - the repository is renamed pst-numeric (it was
                   postscript-math) and its files are sorted into
                   source/, test/, examples/ and tools/
                 - 6 new tests for the namespace (581 in all); the tests
                   run against the .ps files and the headers, and pass
                   with Ghostscript 9.52 and 10.08

1.1  2026/11     (as postscript-math)
                 - Matrix.ps: mfromrows, mtorows, mcopy, midentity,
                   mtranspose, madd, msub, mscale, mdet, minv, msolve,
                   mlstsq, meigsym, mPrint; every operation accepts bignum
                   and decimal-string elements
                 - bignumlibrary.ps: sqrtbn, expbn, powbn, atanbn, asinbn,
                   acosbn, atan2bn, sinhbn, coshbn, tanhbn, factbn,
                   binombn; typchk recognises complex numbers
                 - new: Complex.ps (complex numbers) and Numeric.ps (roots,
                   integrals, polynomials, gcd and lcm)
                 - 253 new tests (575 in all)

1.0  2026/11     (as postscript-math)
                 - bignumlibrary.ps rewritten with the same number format;
                   subbn, mulbn and setbn fixed; added divbn, the
                   comparisons, negbn, absbn, truncbn, roundbn, bniszero,
                   bncvs, bncvr, sinbn, cosbn, tanbn, lnbn, log10bn, pibn;
                   default precision 20 digits
                 - Trig.ps rewritten from the CORDIC algorithm; fixes the
                   signs of corcos and cortan and coratan for x > 0, y < 0
                 - Matrix.ps: removed a stray showpage
                 - licensed under the LPPL 1.3c

0.5  2012        first version (bignumlibrary.ps, Trig.ps, Matrix.ps)
